Total pounds to be distributed = Number of restaurants * Pounds of carrots per restaurant
Total pounds to be distributed = 40 * 2
Total pounds to be distributed = 80 pounds

Now, we subtract the total pounds to be distributed from the total pounds available to find out how many pounds will not be used.

Total pounds available = 200 pounds
Total pounds to be distributed = 80 pounds

Pounds of carrots not to be used = Total pounds available - Total pounds to be distributed
Pounds of carrots not to be used = 200 - 80
Pounds of carrots not to be used = 120 pounds

