Remaining students = 1000 - 300 = 700 students.
3. Then, 3/5 of the remaining students exited through exit B:
3/5 of 700 = (3/5) × 700 = 420 students exited through B.
Remaining students after exits A and B = 700 - 420 = 280 students.
4. Since all the remaining students after A and B exits went out through exit C, the number of students who went out through exit C is 280.
#### 280",appraisal
