Step 2: Find out how many non-work emails she sends.
Total emails = 16
Non-work emails = Total emails - Work emails = 16 - 7 = 9
Step 3: Find out how many emails she sends to her family.
Two-thirds of the non-work emails are to family.
Emails to family = (2/3) * Non-work emails = (2/3) * 9 = 6
Step 4: Find out how many emails are neither work nor family.
Emails remaining = Non-work emails - Emails to family = 9 - 6 = 3
Step 5: Find out how many emails she sends to her boyfriend.
One-third of the other emails are to her boyfriend.
Emails to boyfriend = (1/3) * Emails remaining = (1/3) * 3 = 1
